WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.550
Narrator: When Charlize
Theron played Megyn Kelly

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.260
in "Bombshell," the
makeup team had to change

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.193
the very structure of Theron's face,

00:00:08.193 --> 00:00:09.901
right down to her nose.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:13.850
Makeup artist Kazu Hiro gave
Theron two hidden nose plugs

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.580
tailored to widen her nostrils
to match Kelly's face.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.470
It's just one of the many
details productions tackle

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.100
when transforming actors
into real public figures,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.270
because unlike fictional characters,

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.470
audiences already know what
these characters look like,

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.295
so they can easily catch any mistake.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.880
Rami Malek's Oscar-winning
portrayal of Freddie Mercury

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.270
in "Bohemian Rhapsody" needed to capture

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.780
one very unique physical feature:

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.720
the Queen front man's iconic teeth.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.230
So Malek wore fake teeth

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.490
to account for Mercury's
additional four incisors.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.840
And the teeth had to be
adjusted and resized perfectly

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.660
so they didn't change
the way Malek talked.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.770
Since Mercury was a performer,
Malek also had to move

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.190
and dance on stage the way Mercury did.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:02.610
To achieve this, Malek worked

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.990
with movement director Polly Bennett.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:06.890
First, they studied Mercury's past

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:08.810
and learned that he was both a boxer

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:10.650
and long-distance runner.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.920
So Malek trained himself to be agile

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.570
and limber like a boxer.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:15.780
With this boxing background,

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.840
Mercury could change direction
very quickly on stage.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.660
And so too could Malek.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.240
Meanwhile, the film wanted
to recreate Live Aid

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.650
nearly shot for shot,
meaning Malek had to imitate

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.800
every frame of the concert footage.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.420
You can see Malek perfectly match

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.170
how Mercury handles the mic here

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.870
and how he struts around on stage here.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.750
The makeup team behind "Bombshell"

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.950
had just six weeks of preproduction

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:43.930
to make Charlize Theron
look like Megyn Kelly.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.120
Luckily, Theron didn't
need heavy prosthetics

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.610
for her transformation.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.420
Instead, the team focused
more on subtle differences,

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.050
far beyond the nose plugs
we mentioned earlier.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:56.530
First, Theron and Kelly have
very different-shaped eyes.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.810
So makeup artist Vivian Baker
turned to fake eyelashes,

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.400
using Lashify Gossamers,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.400
which come in pieces
instead of a single strip.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.280
This flexibility gave Baker the ability

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.010
to play with the weight
of Theron's lash line.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:10.470
With the addition of fake eyelids,

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.860
this transformed her eyes,

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.960
according to makeup artist Kazu Hiro,

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.790
from deep-socketed to more hooded.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:19.680
To get a deeper shade of
blue to match Kelly's eyes,

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.060
Theron wore colored contact lenses.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.240
And to match what the
makeup team described

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.270
as Kelly's "heart-shaped face,"

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:28.300
the team lowered Theron's wig,

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.435
thus lowering her hairline.

00:02:30.435 --> 00:02:33.340
Hiro also created some
traditional prosthetics as well,

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.750
like an upturned nose tip

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.417
and angular jaw and chin pieces.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.870
Actor Gary Oldman looks
nothing like Winston Churchill.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.010
So when the actor was
cast to play Churchill

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.160
in "Darkest Hour,"

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.940
makeup artist Kazu Hiro
had to cover Oldman

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.620
in nearly half his body weight

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.960
worth of special effects makeup.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.420
They did about three to five makeup tests,

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.590
matching various silicone prostheses

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.930
to see what was crucial and what wasn't.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.373
Hiro realized he could
cover Oldman's cheeks,

00:03:02.373 --> 00:03:04.610
jowls, neck, chin, and nose.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.910
But Oldman's eyes, mouth, and forehead

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.170
were important for emphasizing
expressions and emotions.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.123
So Hiro intentionally left out

00:03:12.123 --> 00:03:14.340
some of Churchill's physical features,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.468
like discarding the piece

00:03:15.468 --> 00:03:17.820
for Churchill's real-life forehead scar.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.400
That's why you can see
Oldman's real forehead creases

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.370
emote as much as his mouth.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:24.470
The team made up for this
diversion from the truth

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.010
by nailing details the viewer

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.440
might not even think of as essential,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.380
like giving the prosthetic
pieces pink and blotchy tones

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.180
to match the leader's skin.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.102
In the end, even without the scar,

00:03:35.102 --> 00:03:37.960
"Darkest Hour" created
a convincing Churchill,

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.552
leading to Oscar wins
for both Oldman and Hiro.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.760
As seen in "I, Tonya," visual effects

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.410
can be just as crucial to
an actor's transformation

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.110
as makeup and training.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.070
Margot Robbie trained for five months

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:53.710
to skate like Tonya Harding,

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.100
but there were multiple moves

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.780
too difficult for a non-Olympic athlete.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.710
And since Harding's skating routines

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.200
are just as famous as her public persona,

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.900
the film had to get the
moves exactly right.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.891
So the team used two VFX methods

00:04:06.891 --> 00:04:08.865
to seamlessly combine Robbie's training

00:04:08.865 --> 00:04:10.630
with her stunt double's.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:12.710
For the first method, a
stunt double would skate

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:14.890
with an orange tennis ball on her head.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.600
Her face would be
swapped out for Robbie's.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.250
The second method was
full head replacement.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:23.110
They 3D-scanned Robbie's
face to get a full range

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.200
of her skin texture and expressions

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.390
in order to build a digital model.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.723
Head replacement was useful

00:04:28.723 --> 00:04:30.660
for complex shots like this one,

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.200
which was actually three
shots stitched together.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.400
Because of this careful
work behind the scenes,

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.525
you'll never be able to tell

00:04:36.525 --> 00:04:38.000
what part of the shot is Robbie

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.890
and what part is a double.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.710
Instead, you can just focus
on how Robbie imitated

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.270
all of Harding's mannerisms,

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:47.110
from putting her hand over
her face when she's upset

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:50.093
to raising her arms in
a moment of triumph.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.210
In "Rocketman," the first
step to transforming

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.200
Taron Egerton into Elton John

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.940
was nailing the costumes,

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.780
especially when Egerton was performing.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:03.030
After all, John himself
said he doesn't feel

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.513
like the Elton John

00:05:04.513 --> 00:05:07.050
until he chooses his outfit for a show.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.990
So costume designer Julian Day

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.665
closely modeled Egerton's looks

00:05:10.665 --> 00:05:12.990
after John's real outfits.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.390
This included designing
50 pairs of glasses

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:18.400
and 50 pairs of shoes,
one of which was covered

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.650
in real Swarovski crystals.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.760
And while Egerton
already knew how to sing,

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:26.090
playing an instrument in
Elton John's legendary style

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.230
is a whole other skill.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:30.050
Egerton spent six weeks training

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.480
with piano coach Michael L. Roberts.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.000
According to Roberts, a
piano is hard to perform at,

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.380
since you can't move around with it

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:37.840
like you would with a guitar.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.960
So Egerton focused on the unique parts

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.600
of John's playing style,

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.600
such as how he leans into his mic

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.000
and sometimes plays with his feet.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.500
Roberts and Egerton also studied
John's musical influences,

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.230
like blues and boogie-woogie,

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:54.360
to get the right style
of finger placement.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:55.750
Because of that physicality,

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:59.158
it really felt like you were
watching Elton John play.

